WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.550
With a direct call, the caller names the operation
it wants another component to perform.

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:10.976
With implicit invocation, a component announces an
event and registered handlers react.

00:00:10.976 --> 00:00:16.838
A debugger can announce that execution stopped,
letting an editor highlight source without the

00:00:16.838 --> 00:00:20.018
debugger depending on that editor’s implementation.

00:00:20.018 --> 00:00:26.130
The same idea supports user-interface observers and
database triggers inside a single application.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:31.181
An event describes something that happened, such as
a seat becoming available.

00:00:31.181 --> 00:00:37.462
Consumers can react independently: notify a student,
update a dashboard or record an audit trail.

00:00:37.462 --> 00:00:43.355
A publisher-subscriber intermediary routes events to
interested subscriptions, reducing the

00:00:43.355 --> 00:00:46.464
producer’s need to track every consumer address.

00:00:46.464 --> 00:00:52.875
Topics and filters let consumers select relevant
changes without requiring a new direct integration

00:00:52.875 --> 00:00:54.688
for each interested service.
